<title>USA: Andean Development changes proposed IPO terms.</title>
<headline>Andean Development changes proposed IPO terms.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1996-11-06</dateline>
<text>
<p>Andean Development Corp's has changed the terms of its initial public offering, increaseing the number of shares to be offered to 1.2 million from one million shares, according to lead underwriter Barron Chase Securities.</p>
<p>The company plans to offer the shares for $5 each on the Nasdaq National Market under the symbol &quot;ADCC&quot;, according to a regulatory filing. It will also offer 1.2 million warrants.</p>
</text>
